This project is a monorepo managed by pnpm and nx/lerna.

The root of the monorepo is src folder (which is not the git root). The builds folder contains the builds for the different platforms.
Currently, only the darwin build is supported, but in future Windows will be supported as well.
The code in the @trici/desktop package is built for prod (js bundle and swift console apps) and then copied to the builds/darwin folder.


The docs folder contains the documentation for the project.
.
├── builds
│   └── darwin
├── docs
├── src
│   ├── node_modules
│   ├── packages
│   └── scripts
└── venv
    ├── bin
    ├── include
    └── lib



Each package has its own tests which is located in the __tests__ folder. For example:

├── packages
│   ├── activmon
│   │   ├── __tests__
│   │   ├── dist
│   │   └── src
│   ├── app-observer
│   │   ├── __tests__
│   │   ├── bin
│   │   │   └── dev
│   │   ├── dist
│   │   ├── logs
│   │   └── src
│   │       └── swift


The @trici/dal package is the data access layer and provides a the interface to conduct database operations. To independently
test the data access layer,the migrations are located in the __tests__/knex/migrations folder. This is a mirror of the actual migrations
folder which is location in the @trici/desktop package in the knex/migrations folder.

All the repository save methods should return the object that was saved, rather than just the id or void.

The migration files are named in the format of YYYYMMDD_001_migration_name.js. The YYYYMMDD is the timestamp(year, month, day) of the migration and the 001 is the migration number.

